  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Ending AIDS as a Public Health Threat by 2030</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Ending AIDS as a Public Health Threat by 2030.The Global Fund&#x2019;s support contributes to the achievement of the overall strategic goal of the Zimbabwe National HIV and AIDS program to end AIDS as a Public Health threat (aligned to SDG3) by 2030. To reach this goal, Zimbabwe aims at achieving the following impact results: reduce HIV incidence in Zimbabwe by 60% from 0.48% in 2018 to less than 0.19% by 2026; to reduce AIDS-related deaths to 60% from 21,800 in 2018 to less than 10,464 in 2026; and reduce MTCT rate to less than 5% by 2025. The project will support addressing service delivery gaps and strengthen the capacity of the national program to provide HIV prevention, care, and treatment services in the country. The project will further enhance integration and efficiencies, prioritize key and vulnerable populations and geographic hotspots, and improve quality across the continuum of care.</narrative>
  </description>
